# Goshen Dems Theme Rules

Before editing theme files, read `AGENTS.md` and the relevant doc in `docs/`.

## Required reading by task

- Template/PHP changes → `docs/theme-guide.md`
- ACF fields, CPTs → `docs/content-model.md`
- New story block → `docs/how-to/add-story-block.md`
- Plugins (forms, SEO) → `docs/plugins.md`

## Code conventions

- Escape output: `esc_html`, `esc_url`, `esc_attr`, `wp_kses_post` for WYSIWYG
- Guard ACF fields before access (`is_array`, `! empty()`)
- New flexible content layouts: ACF JSON + `template-parts/content-block-{layout}.php` + CSS
- Enqueue JS/CSS in `functions.php`; do not leave orphan script files
- Prefer ACF field values over hardcoded IDs (forms, page content)
- Use page slug/template ACF location rules, not page IDs

## Local environment

- Theme is symlinked to Local WP — edits here are live
- Use Local Site Shell for WP-CLI, not Homebrew `wp`
- MCP server: `wordpress-goshen-local` in `.cursor/mcp.json` (gitignored)

## Do not

- Commit `.cursor/mcp.json`
- Hardcode Ninja Form IDs when ACF `form_shortcode` exists
- Register CPTs in PHP — use ACF JSON in `acf-json/`
- Assume elected-positions CPT is active (currently inactive in JSON)

## After structural changes

Update `docs/content-model.md` and `docs/audit/changelog.md`.

Known issues: [audit/findings.md](audit/findings.md) · Fix backlog: [audit/summary.md](audit/summary.md)
